/* The handoff's commit row, quoted from `Splice Chamber.dc.html`:
 *
 *     display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 11px; padding: 12px 16px 8px;
 *       <div>  COST  /  <13px charge glyph>  <17px Baloo "2">
 *       <button flex: 1>  Begin Splice
 *
 * THE OUTER PADDING IS NOT HERE. This row goes into
 * `ScreenScaffold.CtaRow`, which already carries the gutter and the top
 * space; adding the handoff's 16px again would inset the button from every
 * card above it by 16 where the scaffold puts everything else at 12. The
 * scaffold's own note on `.screen-scaffold__content` is the same lesson
 * measured the hard way - two containers each applying "the" gutter.
 */
.cost-cta-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.cost-cta-row__block {
    flex-direction: column;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-right: 11px;
}

.cost-cta-row__line {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 2px;
}

/* TWO CLASSES, to beat icons.uss's 19px and --mute-soft without depending on
 * sheet order. The handoff draws this glyph at 13px in the deeper teal it
 * uses for the charge mark everywhere - the same --teal-text the resource
 * pill in the header tints its own charge glyph with, which is what makes
 * the two read as one currency. */
.cost-cta-row .cost-cta-row__icon {
    width: 13px;
    height: 13px;
    margin-right: 5px;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: var(--teal-text);
}

/* TWO CLASSES AGAIN, over `.t-num`'s --text-secondary, and this is the
 * biggest of the three size overrides in this task: 17px against 11. The
 * handoff sets this number at 17px beside a 16px CTA label, so it is the
 * second-largest thing in the row and the only number in it. At 11 it would
 * be smaller than the eyebrow's own tracking makes "COST" look, and the
 * price of the action would read as a footnote to it.
 *
 * --text-cta IS 17px EXACTLY, so this is the scale rather than a literal.
 * The floor is a minimum and going up does not touch bible 10.6;
 * verify-uss-tokens.sh check 2 reads for --text-micro under a `.t-num`
 * selector, which is the thing the floor actually forbids. */
.cost-cta-row .cost-cta-row__cost {
    font-size: var(--text-cta);
    color: var(--ink);
}

/* `flex-basis: 0` as well as `flex-grow: 1`, so the button takes the row's
 * remaining width rather than its own content width plus the remainder - a
 * long CTA label ("See the lineage") and a short one ("Start") end at the
 * same right edge, which is what makes a column of screens look like one
 * app.
 *
 * THE VERTICAL MARGIN IS ZEROED. Theme.uss gives every Button 4px top and
 * bottom for a stacked CTA column; in a row beside a two-line cost block it
 * only makes the row 8px taller than the taller of its two children. */
.cost-cta-row__cta {
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-shrink: 1;
    flex-basis: 0;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;
}
